      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To manage risk over vast distances, merchants often utilized systems of bills of exchange, which functioned as early forms of checks or promises of payment. Investors and powerful trading communities helped develop rudimentary credit networks, allowing merchants to purchase goods in one territory and settle the debt using currency or goods from another. This system reduced the dangerous need to carry large amounts of precious metal across unstable routes.",
